From: MGS2 RG353VS compatibility port
Subject: [PATCH] libdg: make fixed-function wpatch own its UV transform mode

Apply after 02-wpatch-consumer-and-state-isolation.patch.

Every fixed-function wpatch variant uploads a stage-0 texture matrix, but the
renderer never selects the corresponding D3DTTFF_COUNT2 transform mode. Other
renderers can leave that stage disabled or projected, making the water's UV
matrix depend on draw order. Select COUNT2 on entry to the non-shader branch so
the matrix and the mode have the same owner.

The live FINALPLAY21 DG_WinApp flag has bit 8 clear, so the global device init
also selects COUNT2 and the material/colour-source setup. That refutes a missing
material setup on this route, but it does not protect wpatch from later EVM or
shadow/optical renderer state changes.

The distributed game executable is not stored here. A separate fail-closed
helper validates the exact legal input and code bytes, emits the equivalent
temporary-image trampoline, and verifies its complete output hash.

--- a/mgs2x/source/system/libdg/wpatch.c
+++ b/mgs2x/source/system/libdg/wpatch.c
@@ -1227,6 +1227,9 @@
 		FMATRIX	mtx ;
 
 		/* VertexShader非対応版 */
+		DG_SetTextureStageState(0, D3DTSS_TEXTURETRANSFORMFLAGS,
+				D3DTTFF_COUNT2) ;
+
 #if FALSE
 		mtx = DG_UnitMatrix ;
 		mtx.m[0][0] = patch->tex->tex_trans.vec1.x ;
